- Platform admin REST resource now expects the new `TenantLifecycleRequest` payload for suspend/reactivate, exposes plan retrieval/change endpoints, adds impersonation renewal, and consistently emits RFC‑7807 errors (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/platformops/api/rest/PlatformAdminResource.java:254-465`). Supporting DTOs (`TenantLifecycleRequest`, `PlanChangeRequest`, `TenantPlanInfo`, `PlatformMetricsResponse`, and the expanded `ImpersonationContext`) live under `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/platformops/api/types/`.
- Tenant lifecycle actions now toggle emergency kill-switch feature flags and log ticket numbers via `PlatformAdminService` (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/platformops/services/PlatformAdminService.java:160-307`), while `StoreMetricsService` aggregates KPIs from `SalesByPeriodAggregate` read models and enforces date validation (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/platformops/services/StoreMetricsService.java:63-161`).
- Impersonation lifecycle enforces a two-hour TTL with auto-expiration, renewal, and audit logging through `ImpersonationService` plus the new `ImpersonationSessionRepository.findExpiredSessions` helper (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/platformops/services/ImpersonationService.java:75-333`, `.../data/repositories/ImpersonationSessionRepository.java:7-44`).
- Integration tests cover the new behaviors: kill-switch enforcement, plan management, impersonation renewal/expiry, and error payloads in `PlatformAdminResourceIT` (`modules/core-platform/src/test/java/villagecompute/storefront/platformops/api/rest/PlatformAdminResourceIT.java:83-360`). 
- Documentation and specs now match the new contracts: `/api/v1/openapi.yaml:400-650` (and mirrored `modules/core-platform/api/v1/openapi.{yaml,json}`) document all platform admin endpoints/schemas; the ad-hoc `api/v1/platform-admin-endpoints.yaml` file was removed; `docs/platform/console.md:103-166` describes ticket requirements, kill switches, and the renew endpoint; `.codemachine/artifacts/tasks/tasks_I5.json` marks `I5.T1` complete.

